==================================================
25. KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
==================================================

1. Random Forest Regression is a supervised learning
   algorithm for predicting a continuous target.

2. It is an ENSEMBLE of Decision Trees.

3. It builds MANY Decision Trees.

4. It introduces randomness through:
   → Bootstrap samples
   → Random feature subsets

5. For regression, the final prediction is commonly the
   average of the predictions from all trees.

6. n_estimators controls the number of trees.

7. max_depth controls tree depth.

8. Random Forest generally does not require feature scaling.

9. It can model nonlinear relationships.

10. It generally reduces the high variance of a single
    Decision Tree through averaging.

11. OOB samples are observations not selected in a tree's
    bootstrap sample and can be used for an OOB performance
    estimate.

12. Random Forest is less interpretable than a single
    Decision Tree.

13. Main idea:

    MANY DECISION TREES
            ↓
      DIFFERENT TREES
            ↓
       PREDICTIONS
            ↓
         AVERAGE
            ↓
     FINAL PREDICTION